;; manifest/ipni-publisher.edn — the IPNI publisher identity for this workspace.
;;
;; ADR-2608160300 recorded that nothing can be announced without a
;; /p2p/{peer-id}, and named this file as the artifact that unblocks the rest
;; of the line. Owner instruction 2026-08-26 ("できるように整えていって") is the
;; authorization; the two decisions it recorded are answered below.
;;
;; This file carries PUBLIC values only. The seed is in kagi, by name.
{;; The identity that SIGNS the live head. Read off the wire, not asserted:
 ;; GET https://ipni.kotobase.net/ipni/v1/head -> {"pubkey":{"/":{"bytes": …}}},
 ;; identity-multihash that protobuf key, base58btc it. Measured 2026-08-31.
 ;;
 ;; This field was stale by two rotations until then. It named the 2026-08-27
 ;; key while the head had been signed by another since 2026-08-30, and a
 ;; fourth identity was never recorded at all -- see :identity-history. The
 ;; file that exists to say which key publishes did not know which key was
 ;; publishing, and nothing compared the two. `scripts/verify-ipni-publisher-record.cljs`
 ;; now does.
 :ipni.publisher/peer-id "12D3KooWGxKwrwhqzVDKynC6PzP3vSWC5F3JjjmaqWyTE91YBt7X"

 ;; The same Ed25519 key seen through the IPNS naming plane. Recorded so the
 ;; two derivations can be cross-checked without holding the seed: decoding
 ;; this name yields the public key the peer-id is built from.
 ;;
 ;; Derivation (verified 2026-08-31 by reproducing the PREVIOUS recorded pair
 ;; from its own peer-id before applying it to this one -- a derivation that
 ;; cannot reproduce a known-good pair may not be used to write a new one):
 ;;   multihash = 0x00 <len> <protobuf pubkey>       (identity)
 ;;   peer-id   = base58btc(multihash)
 ;;   ipns-name = "k" + base36(0x01 0x72 <multihash>) (CIDv1, libp2p-key)
 :ipni.publisher/ipns-name "k51qzi5uqu5ditqo6wh890it27iac9968e2q9jhijcqhnmfok6bmbiceqvodra"

 ;; Custody. Taken one item at a time by this identifier -- never enumerated.
