 ;; ── ADR-2608160300's own success criterion, run end to end on one CID ──
 ;;
 ;; The ADR asks for four things and says the fourth is not optional:
 ;; advertise, see the index hand back kotobase's multiaddr, fetch from that
 ;; address and re-hash, then IsRm and watch it go. "3 が無い advertise は
 ;; 緑にしない."
 ;;
 ;;   2026-09-01T05:29Z  advertised. cid.contact indexed it in 15s and
 ;;                      returned kotobase alongside the three third parties.
 ;;   2026-09-01T05:33Z  fetched from that address; the bytes re-hashed to
 ;;                      the CID that was asked for.
 ;;   2026-09-01T05:45Z  two removals published, both synced. Five minutes
 ;;                      later the entry was still listed, so the run was
 ;;                      recorded NOT green rather than rounded up.
 ;;   2026-09-01T12:07Z  it is gone. Six and a half hours, not five minutes.
 ;;
 ;; An absence is only evidence if the instrument can see a presence, so the
 ;; measurement carries two controls and reports :unmeasured -- never :ok --
 ;; when either is missing:
 ;;
 ;;   the witness multihash still returns its three third-party providers,
 ;;   so the index has not merely forgotten the multihash; and
 ;;
 ;;   the same matcher, on the same surface, still finds kotobase at
 ;;   :control-cid, so it is able to see kotobase at all.
 ;;
 ;; Without the second control this check would report success from a typo in
 ;; a peer id. verify-ipni-publisher-record.cljs re-measures all three every
 ;; six hours; this file records what they said, not a promise about them.
 :ipni.publisher/lifecycle-proof
 {:status :ok
  :hypothesis "ipni-h1 (discoverable-as-provider)"
  :adr "ADR-2608160300"
  :surface "https://cid.contact/multihash/{base58btc-multihash}"   ; the uncached one
  :provider "12D3KooWGmq2x23J59LmqyBT5ik8pK9gEz7N3Y4vdJidezf7Usz3"
